{
  "requirement": "Every {term}`requirements.sdk.application_domain` implements\n`trust_but_verify::domain::Domain`. A domain is cloneable and safe to share between\nexecutions. The following chapters introduce its members one capability at a\ntime.\n\n```rust,ignore\npub trait Domain: Clone + Send + Sync {\n    type Error: Send;\n    type NodeData: Clone + Eq + Hash + Send + Sync;\n    type NodeContent: NodeContents;\n    type EdgeLabel: Clone + Send + Sync;\n\n    fn cache(&self) -> &ValidationCache<Self>;\n    fn node_path(&self, node: &NodeId<Self>) -> NodePath;\n    fn node_content(\n        &self,\n        node: &NodeId<Self>,\n    ) -> Result<Self::NodeContent, Self::Error>;\n    fn outgoing_edges(\n        &self,\n        node: &NodeId<Self>,\n        label: Self::EdgeLabel,\n    ) -> Result<Vec<NodeId<Self>>, Self::Error>;\n    fn load_evidence(\n        &self,\n        node: &NodeId<Self>,\n        criterion: &CriterionPath,\n    ) -> impl Future<Output = Result<Option<Record<Self::NodeData, Self::EdgeLabel>>, Self::Error>> + Send;\n    fn store_evidence(\n        &self,\n        node: &NodeId<Self>,\n        criterion: &CriterionPath,\n        record: &Record<Self::NodeData, Self::EdgeLabel>,\n    ) -> impl Future<Output = Result<(), Self::Error>> + Send;\n\n    fn project_sources(&self) -> Option<SourceProject<Self>> { ... }\n    fn source_node(\n        &self,\n        item: &OutlineData,\n    ) -> Result<Self::NodeData, SourceError> { ... }\n    fn source_address(&self, _data: &Self::NodeData) -> Option<OutlineData> { ... }\n}\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The tests adequately check `requirements.sdk.domain`.\n\n**Obligations.** The text requires four things:\n- Every application domain implements `Domain`.\n- A domain is cloneable and safe to share between executions (`Clone + Send + Sync`).\n- The trait declares the associated types with their bounds: `Error: Send`, `NodeData: Clone + Eq + Hash + Send + Sync`, `NodeContent: NodeContents`, and `EdgeLabel: Clone + Send + Sync`.\n- The trait declares the listed method signatures. `load_evidence` and `store_evidence` return `Send` futures. `project_sources`, `source_node` and `source_address` are defaulted.\n\n**Main test.** `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs#fn[domain_relationships_accept_opaque_types_and_send_only_errors]` covers the type-level contract.\n- It implements `Domain` for a fixture whose `NodeData` and `EdgeLabel` are opaque types and whose `Error` is `Send` but not `Sync` (it wraps a `Cell`). A stricter bound on `Error` would therefore fail to compile.\n- The generic `check_bounds<G: Domain>` helper compiles checks for `G: Clone + Send + Sync`, for `NodeData: Clone + Eq + Hash + Send + Sync`, for `EdgeLabel: Clone + Send + Sync`, and for `Error: Send`. It also checks `NodeContent: NodeContents`. Loosening any required bound would break compilation.\n- The `send(...)` helper checks that the `load_evidence` and `store_evidence` futures are `Send` even though the error is not `Sync`.\n- It calls `node_content`, `node_path`, `outgoing_edges`, `load_evidence` and `store_evidence` with the declared signatures and asserts their results. That includes an error from `outgoing_edges`, duplicate and empty successor lists, and distinct node paths.\n- It asserts that the default `project_sources` returns `None` and that the default `source_node` returns `SourceError::Invalid`.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs#fn[domain_without_project_sources_leaves_source_tools_disabled]` asserts that the default `source_address` returns `None`. It carries no `{test}` reference to this requirement. The text specifies no behavior for the defaults beyond their signatures, so this is not a gap.\n\n**Safe to share between executions.** Several tests run one domain in concurrent executions and assert separate traces and records:\n- `concurrent_single_node_validations_keep_separate_traces`\n- `concurrent_same_criterion_executions_keep_complete_independent_records`\n- `concurrent_tool_agents_isolate_histories_pages_and_submissions_and_share_reads`\n- `shared_context_allows_independent_concurrent_agent_calls`\n- `later_lighter_agent_calls_preserve_the_contexts_existing_trace` also asserts that the context is `Send + Sync`.\n\n**Implementing the trait in real domains.** Further tests use domain implementations through the trait:\n- `criteria_keep_typed_answers_and_persist_only_when_requested`\n- `deterministic_validation_uses_required_storage_without_an_agent`\n- `behavioral_adequacy_uses_domain_contents_and_returns_a_typed_fingerprinted_answer`\n- `contexts_render_once_allow_non_send_values_and_hash_exact_prefix_text`\n- `src/sdk.rs#mod[tests]/fn[domain_formats_supplied_contents_without_resolving_a_replacement]`, which does so for the habeas domain.\n\n`public_exports_match_the_appendix` tests the public export inventory, not this requirement's behavior.\n\nI found no gaps and no marking gaps. No `{fixme}` acknowledgments apply.",
  "references": "def95cddcfd729d8ab2a7869cd3b7c1d236dc0d2686efb64ec30c6a98a2e742a",
